== History ==
[[File:12 26 Sand Bridge.png|thumb|<small>Coco in Awe of the Sand Bridge</small>]]
This spell is first seen used by [[Olruggio]] after the [[Staircase River]] dries up and is reduced to nothing but sand. As the original bridge had collapsed, he creates a bridge of sand using magic as a temporary solution.{{Ref|m|12|26-27}}{{Ref|a|8}}

[[Agott]], having paid close attention to Olruggio's Casting Seal,{{Ref|m|33|9}} uses this spell in the [[Argentgard]] in an attempt to surprise [[Beldaruit]] of the [[Three Wise|Wise]] and pass her retaking of the [[Pentacle of Proving|test]] for the [[Sincerity of the Shield]].{{Ref|[[Archives of Witch Hat Atelier]], Page 148}} She claims it is the most difficult spell she's learned to date. This attempt fails and Beldaruit later combines the effects of Agott and her fellow apprentices' spells to cast a spell of his own: The [[Playland of Sand]].{{Ref|m|33|8-13}}

Beldaruit is not awed by the Agott's display because of the spell's practical use and necessity, thus making it a common spectacle he is already familiar with.{{Ref|m|33|10}} This suggests that this spell is well-known enough to be used often by [[witches]] helping [[outsiders]] in need.
